L554@P7: negative correlation suggests that, given a fixed computational budget (i.e., number of iterations), it is less likely to
L555@P7: discover the optimal features as p grows. We hypothesize
L556@P7: that extending the number of iterations would allow for a
L557@P7: more thorough exploration of this larger space, potentially
L558@P7: mitigating this negative effect.
L559@P7: 5.2. Qualitative Analysis
L560@P7: In both tasks, the agents demonstrated appropriate tool use,
L561@P7: requesting external information when necessary. For instance, in the jungle chess dataset, we observe the Scientist Agent requested an overview of the game’s rules, and
